<article class="env-lemma" id="04WD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04WD">Lemma <span data-tag="04WD">8.12.3</span>.</a> Let $u : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}$ be a continuous functor of sites. Let $p : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{D}$ be a stack in groupoids over $\mathcal{D}$. Then $u^ p\mathcal{S}$ is a stack in groupoids over $\mathcal{C}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/04WC" data-tag="04WC">8.12.2</a> and the fact that all fibre categories are groupoids. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>